  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we see that as $x$ decreases to $-\\infty ,$ the graph of the function moves closer to the horizontal asymptote $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, as $x$ approaches $-\\infty ,$ the function $f(x)$ approaches $2,$ and we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=2.\n$$",
